Assertions:
[NAV] the "All orders" link lands on /company/my-customers/@td(ORG_TECHFLOW.platform_id)/orders -- the customer-scoped route, never /company/customer-orders (cross-customer) and never /account/orders (buyer route) {SPEC}
[STATE] the breadcrumb on the landing page names @td(ORG_TECHFLOW.name) as its own segment, distinct from the generic "Sales Rep hub" and "My customers" segments {SPEC}
[REL] every rendered order number on the landing page belongs to {@td(ORDER_REP_PLACED.number), @td(ORDER_BUYER_PLACED.number)} or another TechFlow order -- @td(ORDER_NOT_SERVED.number) is absent from every screen this journey visits {BL}
[STATE] both @td(ORDER_REP_PLACED.number) and @td(ORDER_BUYER_PLACED.number) are present in the rendered set before any filter is applied -- the buyer-placed order proves scope is membership-based, not creator-based {BL}
[REL] where a Customer column is rendered, every value in it reads @td(ORG_TECHFLOW.name) -- no other customer leaks into this scoped view {BL}
[STATE] applying the status filter, then sorting, then paging to page 2 never re-admits @td(ORDER_NOT_SERVED.number) and never widens the scope back to the cross-customer route (URL still carries @td(ORG_TECHFLOW.platform_id)) {BL}
[NAV] opening @td(ORDER_REP_PLACED.number) lands on /account/orders/<id> with Pay now and Reorder both enabled {SPEC}
[NAV] opening @td(ORDER_BUYER_PLACED.number) does NOT land on /account/orders/<id> -- it opens the hub's read-only order page, whose only enabled action is Print {SPEC}
[NAV] clicking the breadcrumb's customer segment returns to @td(ORG_TECHFLOW.name)'s profile URL, with its Orders context still active, not the profile's bare default landing state {SPEC}

[NAV] the mouse click on the customer breadcrumb segment lands on /company/my-customers/@td(ORG_TECHFLOW.platform_id) {SPEC}
[REL] activating the same segment by keyboard (Tab + Enter) lands on the identical URL as the mouse click {SPEC}
[DOM] the breadcrumb segment shows a visible focus indicator while it holds keyboard focus {SPEC}

[NAV] the resulting URL is the same customer profile URL recorded before the excursion {SPEC}
[REL] the Recent-Orders block's viewport position and its rendered row set are identical before and after the excursion to the orders list -- asserted as a pre/post relation because that block sits at the top of the profile's main content, so 'positioned at Recent Orders' is not on its own falsifiable {OBSERVED}
[STATE] the profile's own Recent Orders block shows the same content it showed before the excursion -- the filter/sort/page state applied on the full list does not leak back into the profile's own summary block {SPEC}

[STATE] the active page indicator reads page 1 immediately after the narrower filter is applied, not page 3 {BL}
[REL] ORDER_NARROWED_FIRST != ORDER_PAGE3_FIRST -- the grid re-fetched page 1 of the new filter rather than continuing to display the stale page-3 result set relabeled as page 1 {BL}
[STATE] the rendered row count is non-zero when the narrowed filter has at least one matching order -- the grid does not show an empty result purely because it stayed on page 3 of a now-shorter result set {BL}

[REL] the set of order numbers on page 2 is disjoint from the set on page 1 -- no order number appears on both pages {OBSERVED}
[REL] the deduplicated union of the page-1 and page-2 order-number sets has the same cardinality as the sum of the two pages' row counts -- confirming no row silently disappears between the pages either {OBSERVED}
[NET] the page-2 request's after argument is a numeric offset equal to the number of rows already rendered (page size x pages consumed), NOT an opaque edge cursor -- the storefront pages salesRepCustomerOrders by index, so the upstream edge-cursor off-by-one is unreachable from this UI {OBSERVED}

Preconditions:
[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORG_TECHFLOW.platform_id) has a known first and last order in its history; live-discover their created dates. The rep's effective timezone offset is recorded so the boundary-day distinction is observable.

Assertions:
[STATE] the order created on D_FIRST is present in the filtered results {BL}
[STATE] the order created on D_LAST is present in the filtered results {BL}
[MATH] RENDERED_ROW_COUNT = TOTAL_ORDERS_IN_WINDOW -- none excluded purely because its creation timestamp falls on a range boundary day {BL}

[DOM] the empty-state heading/body communicates that the rep serves no customers -- not a generic "no results match your filters" message {BL}
[DOM] no "Clear filters"/"Reset" button or link element is present anywhere in the empty-state region, since no filter was ever applied {BL}
[STATE] no infinite spinner or blank page is shown in place of the empty state {BL}

Preconditions:
[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORDER_BUYER_PLACED.number) was placed by a buyer in @td(ORG_TECHFLOW.platform_id), a customer SR_REP_PRIMARY serves.

Assertions:
[NAV] the destination URL matches /company/my-customers/<org>/orders/<id> (the hub's read-only route) {SPEC}
[REL] the destination URL is never /account/orders/<id> -- the buyer-facing route is unreachable via this row {SPEC}
[STATE] the Pay-now control is never present, enabled, or clickable anywhere on the page {BL}
[STATE] the Reorder control is never present, enabled, or clickable anywhere on the page {BL}
[STATE] Print is the only enabled action control on the page {SPEC}

Preconditions:
[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORDER_REP_PLACED.number) was placed by SR_REP_PRIMARY in @td(ORG_TECHFLOW.platform_id).

[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORDER_BUYER_PLACED.id) belongs to a customer SR_REP_PRIMARY serves but was placed by a buyer, not the rep -- the rep is neither the order's own customer, an org member, nor an administrator.

Assertions:
[DOM] the status-chip element's text content does NOT match the raw-enum regex shape (a bare word like 'New' with no surrounding text) and does NOT match the untranslated-i18n-key regex shape (a string starting with 'sales-rep.') {BL}
[DOM] the first row's Date cell and Total cell text use the selected locale's date and currency format (day/month order, decimal and thousands separators) rather than the default locale's format string {BL}
[STATE] the markup-bearing search term never triggers a live script execution -- no new console error and no alert dialog appears after submission {BL}
[DOM] after submitting a markup-bearing search term, the orders-grid region contains zero elements matching 'img[src*=onerror]' and zero matching 'script', its empty-state element carries a reset/clear-search control, no dialog is raised, and the console error count is unchanged from the pre-search baseline. The term is never echoed back, so there is no escaped sequence to assert on {OBSERVED}

[STATE] the customer scope (@td(ORG_TECHFLOW.platform_id)) is preserved after the reload -- the grid never widens to the cross-customer view {SPEC}
[STATE] EITHER the filter and sort are restored exactly as recorded, OR the page degrades to a named safe default (unfiltered, default sort) while staying on the correct customer scope -- landing on a DIFFERENT, unrequested filter/sort is the failure this case exists to catch {OBSERVED}
[REL] after the reload the rendered row count equals the route's default page size and the first row is the most recent by createdDate -- phrased on the branch that actually occurs, because filter/sort are never restored on this build and an 'if restored' clause is vacuous {OBSERVED}

[STATE] the drawer opened on @td(ORG_ACME.platform_id)'s list does not silently keep showing @td(ORG_TECHFLOW.platform_id)'s prior status options and counts -- it either shows Acme's own options or visibly indicates the facet data is loading/unavailable {OBSERVED}
[DOM] when the facet request is blocked or slow, the drawer's status-option list area shows a skeleton/spinner element or an inline error-message element -- not the previous org's option list with no loading/error indicator present {HYPOTHESIS}
[STATE] no status chip in the drawer, present or stale, causes a filter to be silently applied against the wrong customer's data {OBSERVED}

[SHIFT] no unexpected layout shift occurs while the drawer opens at either viewport {BL}
[TOUCH] every interactive control in the drawer (checkboxes, Apply, Reset, date inputs) measures at least 24x24px at 375px (WCAG 2.2 SC 2.5.8) {BL}
[OVERFLOW] the Apply and Reset buttons are fully contained within the visible viewport at 375px -- neither is clipped nor requires horizontal scroll to reach {BL}
[SPACING] the measured gap between adjacent status checkboxes matches a value in SPACING_GRID_PX (scripts/lib/design-tokens.generated.ts) rather than an ad hoc value -- the constant is named, never a transcribed number {OBSERVED}
[ALIGN] every keyboard-focused control in the Tab walk shows a visible focus indicator, in order: status checkboxes -> date inputs -> Reset -> Apply {BL}
[STATE] the axe-core scan reports zero critical/serious violations for the open drawer at both viewports {BL}

[NAV] Back lands on the customer-orders list, not a blank page or a router error {SPEC}
[REL] POST_BACK_ROWS either equals PRE_BACK_ROWS, or equals the route's unfiltered default first page -- never a third, silently-different row set. The equality-only form contradicted this case's own degrade allowance {OBSERVED}
[REL] POST_BACK_CHIPS equals PRE_BACK_CHIPS -- the previously applied status filter is still active, or (per SR-CO-014's own contract) degrades to a named safe default, never a silently DIFFERENT filter {HYPOTHESIS}

[DOM] the order detail page's own heading and order-number text elements are visible in the DOM on the deep-linked load -- the page is not a blank <body>, a router error boundary, or an unhandled-exception overlay {OBSERVED}
[STATE] the page is gated by the same route guard as reaching it via the list (SalesRep.Enabled + sales-rep:access) -- a deep link is not a way to bypass the gate {BL}
[REL] DEEP_ORDER equals CLICK_ORDER and DEEP_STATUS equals CLICK_STATUS -- the deep-linked render is not a different or stale record than the one reached via the normal click-through path {OBSERVED}
[REL] DEEP_BREADCRUMB equals CLICK_BREADCRUMB and both name @td(ORG_TECHFLOW.name) -- the deep-linked breadcrumb is not a blank or placeholder segment {SPEC}

[STATE] when the order page is mounted (its own heading/order-number elements present), the list page's own grid-header element is never present in the DOM {OBSERVED}
[STATE] when the list page is mounted instead, the order page's own heading element is never present in the DOM {OBSERVED}
[STATE] no order-related mutation is duplicated -- since this surface is read-only, the specific risk here is a stuck loading state or a corrupted route, not a double-submit {HYPOTHESIS}
[NAV] after the refresh settles, the URL is a valid, navigable route -- not a blank or 500 intermediate state {OBSERVED}

[DOM] a graceful re-authentication prompt or a redirect to sign-in is visible -- a raw unhandled 401, a blank page, and a permanently spinning grid are all absent {BL}
[DOM] no raw GraphQL error object, stack frame, or HTTP status code is visible to the customer {BL}
[NAV] after re-authenticating, the rep lands back on the customer-orders route rather than a generic dashboard {HYPOTHESIS}

[DOM] a blocked orders request replaces only the grid's own container with an inline error-message element, while the header nav, breadcrumb links, and filters-drawer trigger remain present and clickable elsewhere on the page {HYPOTHESIS}
[DOM] a forced 500 renders an error-message element together with a "Retry"/"Try again" button, not an empty <body> or a blank grid container {HYPOTHESIS}
[STATE] BASELINE_ROWS are never shown again once the 500/malformed-JSON error state renders -- the grid does not fall back to stale previously-loaded rows instead of the error state {HYPOTHESIS}
[STATE] a malformed-JSON response does not throw an unhandled parse error that crashes the page -- it degrades to the same scoped error state, with no new unhandled-rejection console entry {HYPOTHESIS}

[OVERFLOW] every control (filters, Apply, order rows, Print) remains reachable and unclipped at 200% and 400% zoom {HYPOTHESIS}
[DOM] under prefers-color-scheme: dark, the grid's row text and the breadcrumb link text both render with a contrast ratio >=4.5:1 against their background (WCAG 1.4.3) -- no text element renders in the same or a near-identical color as its background {BL}
[DOM] under prefers-reduced-motion: reduce, the filters-drawer open/close transition and any grid loading-skeleton animation are instantaneous or disabled -- clicking Apply/Reset does not require waiting on a CSS transitionend event to become clickable again {HYPOTHESIS}
[DOM] the print rendering of the read-only order page shows the order content, not the site nav/header/filters chrome, and the Print control itself is absent from the printed output {HYPOTHESIS}

[DOM] the zero-orders state (SR_REP_NOCUSTOMERS) shows a heading/body-text element containing wording equivalent to "you serve no customers yet" (the same empty-state element established in SR-CO-009) -- not an empty grid container with a header row and zero rows, and not a blank page {BL}
[DOM] the exactly-one-order state renders exactly one grid row and no pagination-control element ('Next'/page-number buttons) is present in the DOM at all {OBSERVED}
[OVERFLOW] the many-orders (multi-page) state holds its column widths and row density -- no column collapses or overlaps at the observed row count {OBSERVED}
[OVERFLOW] the long-title/high-line-item row wraps or truncates its overflowing text with an ellipsis/tooltip rather than clipping it silently or breaking the row's layout {OBSERVED}

[STATE] SEARCH_ROWS contains @td(ORDER_BUYER_PLACED.number) {SPEC}
[REL] SEARCH_ROWS is a strict subset of UNFILTERED_ROWS — the search NARROWED the list rather than returning it unchanged, which is how a no-op search is caught {SPEC}
[STATE] SEARCH_FILTER_ARG is non-empty and carries the searched order number — a request that sent no filter at all proves the box is inert {OBSERVED}
[STATE] both Enter and the search button produce the same SEARCH_ROWS {OBSERVED}
[STATE] NOMATCH_ROWS is empty AND the rendered empty state is the filter-aware "nothing matched" variant offering a way to clear the search, never the generic no-orders state and never a bare blank grid {BL}
[STATE] the no-match result never renders the unfiltered list — a filter-field drift was proven live to yield 0 rows with no error, so a silent fall-back to everything is the opposite failure and equally in scope {OBSERVED}

[REL] ZEROMATCH_FILTER_ARG still carries the APPLIED_STATUS term -- the status filter itself is not dropped by the zero-match date range {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the drawer's status-option group element is present in the DOM for this zero-match query, even though the response's term_facets array is empty {BL}
[DOM] a control that removes APPLIED_STATUS alone is present in the drawer and is distinct from the all-or-nothing Reset control {BL}
[STATE] using that per-filter control (not Reset) re-renders the grid with the date range still active and APPLIED_STATUS cleared {HYPOTHESIS}

[DOM] the empty-state text names or otherwise identifies the applied filter as the cause of the zero rows, not the generic wording SR-CO-009 uses for "the rep has no customers" {BL}
[REL] the zero-match empty-state region contains at least one focusable, interactive clear/reset element -- unlike the zero-customers empty state (SR-CO-009), which per BL-SR-012 has none {BL}
[REL] activating that control restores the rendered row count to UNFILTERED_COUNT and removes the applied filter's chip {HYPOTHESIS}

[STATE] MYCUST_COUNT is a rendered, non-blank numeric figure on the my-customers row {OBSERVED}
[STATE] LIST_TOTAL, summed from the rendered per-status facet counts, is a positive integer {OBSERVED}
[MATH] MYCUST_COUNT <= LIST_TOTAL -- the rep-created subset can never exceed this customer's creator-agnostic total, since BL-SR-002 scopes MYCUST_COUNT to orders the rep created while the customer-scoped list is deliberately creator-agnostic {BL}

[REL] TAB1_ORG_ARG equals @td(ORG_TECHFLOW.platform_id) and TAB2_ORG_ARG equals @td(ORG_BUILDRIGHT.platform_id) -- each tab's own request carries its own route's organizationId {OBSERVED}
[REL] TAB1_POST_ORG_ARG still equals @td(ORG_TECHFLOW.platform_id) after acting in tab 2 -- tab 1's next request is not repointed at tab 2's organization {OBSERVED}
[REL] TAB1_POST_FILTER_ARG still carries tab 1's own applied filter, not tab 2's -- filter state is not shared across tabs of the same session {OBSERVED}
[STATE] TAB1_ROWS never renders any order belonging to @td(ORG_BUILDRIGHT.platform_id), and TAB2_ROWS never renders any order belonging to @td(ORG_TECHFLOW.platform_id) {BL}

[REL] BR_FILTER is not TF_FILTER -- @td(ORG_TECHFLOW.platform_id)'s applied status filter did not carry over to @td(ORG_BUILDRIGHT.platform_id) {OBSERVED}
[STATE] BR_PAGE reads page 1, not the page number reached on the previous customer {BL}
[STATE] the drawer's Reset control is disabled (or otherwise indicates no filter is active) immediately after the switch, since no filter has yet been applied to @td(ORG_BUILDRIGHT.platform_id) {OBSERVED}
[REL] BR_FACETS are @td(ORG_BUILDRIGHT.platform_id)'s own facet counts, not @td(ORG_TECHFLOW.platform_id)'s carried over {OBSERVED}

[MATH] COMBINED_ROWS = STATUS_A_COUNT + STATUS_B_COUNT -- two selected statuses combine as a union, not an intersection {OBSERVED}
[REL] COMBINED_ROWS > STATUS_A_ROWS -- adding the second status strictly widens the result set rather than narrowing or leaving it unchanged {OBSERVED}
[STATE] every status value rendered in the grid's status column after the combined filter is either STATUS_A or STATUS_B -- no third status leaks in and no row from either selected status is missing {OBSERVED}
